# React / TypeScript Frontend Standards
## Component size
Keep components under 200 lines. When a component grows beyond that, extract feature state into a custom hook and sub-components into the same directory.
## State reset
Each feature's reset logic must live in one function, not scattered across multiple handlers.
## Console logging
`console.log` is only allowed behind a dev guard. Never leave it in production paths.
```tsx
if (import.meta.env.DEV) console.log('debug:', value)
```
## String encoding
Always save source files as UTF-8. Use Unicode literals directly: `—`, `✗`, `✓`, `→`.
## Polling loops
All polling intervals must have an explicit terminal condition — a status that stops the poll. Document the terminal states in a comment.
## Error handling in async handlers
Every `async` event handler must have a `try/catch`. Unhandled promise rejections surface as silent failures in production.
